# PRESERVED SCRATCH PROBE — ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES / lr_alt_index_discriminator
# Snapshot of the `scratch` slot (TOOLBOX.md 1.3) taken before restoring the default
# fixture, so the synthetic this leaf reproduces on can be re-run by the next reader:
#   cp docs/tasks/artifacts/engine_universal_services/lr_alt_index_discriminator.ebnf grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf
#   make -C rust SHELL=/bin/bash focus_scratch
#   (cd rust && cargo build --features "generated_parsers ebnf_dual_run" --bin ast_pipeline)
# ⛔ Rebuild ast_pipeline AFTER focus_scratch: the focus target builds the binary BEFORE it
#    regenerates the parser, so a binary built by that run judges the PREVIOUS grammar.
# NOTE: acceptance (g): the ONLY direct alternative sits at position 1, so the hoist must be named _lr_alt2 if the suffix is the alternative index+1

# ==============================================================================
# PGEN scratch slot — a blessed, throwaway probe grammar (PARSE-HARNESS approach 3).
#
# WHAT THIS IS
#   The `scratch` grammar is a first-class registered parser whose grammar body is
#   meant to be OVERWRITTEN freely. It lets you parse an arbitrary input against an
#   arbitrary grammar using the whole shipped `parseability_probe` toolbox — with
#   semantics IDENTICAL to the shipped generated parsers — without the full
#   register→codegen→compile-in ceremony for a one-off probe.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Edit the grammar body below (the entry rule must be named `scratch` so the
#      registered slot stays stable; helper rules can be named anything).
#   2. Regenerate + rebuild:  make -C rust SHELL=/bin/bash focus_scratch
#      then rebuild the probe:  (cd rust && cargo build --release --features generated_parsers --bin parseability_probe)
#   3. Drive it with the full toolbox:
#        parseability_probe --parse scratch <input_file>
#        parseability_probe --parse-dump-ast-pretty scratch <input_file> out.json
#        PGEN_TRACE_VERBOSITY=debug parseability_probe --parse scratch <input_file> --trace-rules scratch
#        ast_pipeline grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf --lint-grammar
#        ast_pipeline grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf --report-certificate-coverage --entry-rule scratch --count 40 --seed 0
#
# IMPORTANT
#   The generated artifacts (generated/scratch_parser.rs, generated/scratch.json) are
#   git-ignored — they never enter the tracked set. THIS file is tracked: it is both
#   the blessed slot AND the committed integration-test fixture proving the slot is
#   authoritative-by-construction. If you edit the body for a probe, restore the
#   default (git checkout grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf) before committing so the
#   scratch integration test keeps passing.
#
# See grammars/scratch/README.md and the "The Parse Harness" chapter in docs/book/.
# ==============================================================================

# PROBE C (ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.21 acceptance (g)) — DISCRIMINATES the `{n}` in `_lr_alt{n}`.
#   Probe B hoisted the alternative at position 0 and emitted `_lr_alt1`, which is equally
#   consistent with two hypotheses: H1 the suffix is the ALTERNATIVE's index+1 (mod.rs:3244), H2 it
#   is a running count of hoists. Here the ONLY direct alternative sits at position 1, so H1
#   predicts `expr_lr_alt2` and H2 predicts `expr_lr_alt1`. One run separates them.

@entry: true
scratch := expr

expr := mulwrap | expr "+" term

mulwrap := expr "*" term

term := "n"
